    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0368" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8836/872: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Braden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-07T23:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>606. Refer your 617, July 28. War Production Board advise that upon application
                    they will grant exemptions from M–63<anchor n="44" xml:id="d378-f1"/> to import
                    Isle of Pines grapefruit. It is expected that grapefruit will be removed from
                    the M–63 List when next amendment is printed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d378-f1" n="44" xml:id="d378-f1-content">
                <p>General Imports Order M–63; 6 <hi rendition="#italic">Federal Register</hi>
                    6796.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
